WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.517
The Constitution began with seven

2
00:00:02.517 --> 00:00:04.099
Fundamental Rights.

3
00:00:04.099 --> 00:00:05.564
Today there are six.

4
00:00:05.564 --> 00:00:07.617
Where did the seventh go?

5
00:00:07.932 --> 00:00:09.646
Equality and freedom.

6
00:00:09.646 --> 00:00:11.134
Against exploitation,

7
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:13.053
and freedom of religion.

8
00:00:13.053 --> 00:00:15.175
Cultural and educational rights,

9
00:00:15.175 --> 00:00:17.181
and the right to constitutional

10
00:00:17.181 --> 00:00:18.289
remedies.

11
00:00:18.633 --> 00:00:20.740
The right to property was

12
00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.335
a Fundamental Right in 1950.

13
00:00:23.335 --> 00:00:26.375
The forty-fourth amendment of 1978

14
00:00:26.375 --> 00:00:27.534
removed it.

15
00:00:27.534 --> 00:00:29.002
It is now a legal

16
00:00:29.002 --> 00:00:31.682
right, under Article 300A.

17
00:00:32.013 --> 00:00:33.572
Article 32 lets you go

18
00:00:33.572 --> 00:00:35.560
straight to the Supreme Court

19
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.459
if a right is violated.

20
00:00:37.459 --> 00:00:39.028
Ambedkar called it the very

21
00:00:39.028 --> 00:00:40.546
soul of the Constitution,

22
00:00:40.546 --> 00:00:41.807
and the very heart of

23
00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:42.573
it.

24
00:00:43.237 --> 00:00:44.508
Your turn.

25
00:00:44.508 --> 00:00:45.637
Where is the right to

26
00:00:45.637 --> 00:00:46.866
property now?
